# GET permission denial → NotFound

When a **GET** (read) endpoint uses `runIfActiveWorkspaceMemberAndPermitted` or `runIfPermitted`, pass `NotFoundException` as the denial exception so lacking permission (or not being an active workspace member) does not reveal that the resource exists.

Mutating endpoints (`POST` / `PATCH` / `DELETE` / etc.) keep the default (`ForbiddenException`).

## Example

See `listDevices` in [`TrackerAdminController`](src/tracker/admin/tracker-admin.controller.ts):

```typescript
const devices =
  await this.permissionService.runIfActiveWorkspaceMemberAndPermitted(
    requestUser,
    ENVOYE_WORKSPACE_CODE,
    PERMISSIONS.MANAGE_DEVICES,
    () => this.trackerService.listDevices(),
    NotFoundException,
  );
```

## Avoid

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — remap ForbiddenException in the controller
try {
  await this.permissionService.runIfActiveWorkspaceMemberAndPermitted(...);
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof ForbiddenException) {
    throw new NotFoundException();
  }
  throw error;
}
```
